Slash Em is not a better Nethack.  I've played Nethack for about 3
years now.  I haven't been playing it the whole time, but every time I
take a break I come back to Nethack.  Because it is fun, interesting,
and full of easter eggs.  Just the other day I discovered a funny
message that I didn't know about.

When I took breaks from Nethack, I tried Slash Em, Angband and Ancient
Domains of Mystery (ADOM).  None of those held my attention.  Angband
is like Diablo without the fun and ADOM I just don't get. It has a
number of quests and goals that span a whole series of locations (One
goal is nearly impossible to acheive yet it is considered "the best
ending"), and I'd rather focus on the Dungeon of Doom.

As for Slash EM, it is a lot harder than Nethack.  If you don't do well
in Nethack, chances are you will do worst in Slash Em.  In SE, you
level slower and the enemies get tougher faster.  There are these
electric bugs at low levels that destroy your rings and wands.  Baby
Dragons show up a lot earlier.  Stuff like that.   The fartherest I
made it was the all orc/goblin castle level playing a Monk (the easiest
class in the game for various reasons).

In SE they removed the mysterious force that teleports you back during
the ascent.  I like that.  They made Hell shorter and gave each Demon
Prince its own level.  I like that too.  (I actually enjoy fighting
Demogorgon).

But they added a lot of classes/races/artifacts.  You can dual wield
artifacts, which I think is too powerful.  Some of the classes don't
make sense to me.  An ice mage is like a regular mage except ... worse
because they cast less spells!  They start with summon freezing sphere!
 I don't like how they rearranged the magic system.  Some of the spells
are in different schools and that doesn't make sense to me.  I don't
understand why Magic Mapping is level 7 in SE, because I can't do Hell
without it.  Too aggravating otherwise.

Some of the items or artifacts don't fit the medieval setting.  One
artifact is the Bat out of Hell and it is ... a base ball bat.  There
are lightsabers in Slash Em.  Why?  I don't know.

Also, they added MORE QUESTS.  Never completed the quest in NH?  Well,
in SE there is the class quest AND the alignment quest.  Vecna is in
there, and there is a beholder.  And now Vlads tower is 3 locked doors
and you can only unlock two of them.  I presuem there is treasure in
there, but I've never made it far in SE.

Also, there are toilets.  Not sure why, but seeing a toliet on screen
is kind of silly IMO.  I guess sinks in a dungeon are silly too, but
I'm biased towards NH.  It's more fun and well-thoughout.



